{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384384-making-a-green-lantern-ring","id":1384384,"title":"Making a Green Lantern ring","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-28T01:48:43-07:00","id":1384384,"title":"Making a Green Lantern ring","content":"Random thought. So I'm an Etherite and want to make a green lantern ring that works &quot;exactly&quot; as portrayed in the comic books or as close to this as possible. How would I go about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T06:34:07-07:00","id":1384401,"title":"","content":"The real issue would be that there's no way to get around needing a certain number of successes to make certain (larger and/or more intricate) constructs, so you wouldn't be able to just produce anything and everything at a moment's notice. Otherwise, I think the most rudimentary version of the effect it would be (in M20 terms) Forces 3/Mind 3/Prime 2 effect--Forces 3/Prime 2 to generate not only the green light of the construct, but also the telekinetic power and <i>force</i> that makes it a &quot;hard light&quot; construct, and lasers; Mind 3 to control it all with your mind. The more legit version would be Forces 5/Mind 3/Prime 2, if only to scale up the power and &quot;oomph&quot; of the telekinesis component, enabling you to lift/withstand more. But you're still going to have the issue of not necessarily being able to generate in just one turn a huge locomotive, or a monstrous, Rob Liefeld/90's-esque laser cannon (as Kyle Raynor was so fond of doing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T06:45:31-07:00","id":1384403,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the thing. Not only am I thinking how to make the green lantern ring effect. I'm trying to figure out how to make the ring itself. Which is something like a semi intelligent wonder that chooses people and responds to the oath and is limited only by the user's imagination and will. <br /> <br /> Given all spheres at 5, unlimited time, and my own sanctum, can I construct it, or would I have to do something as drastic as journey into the Umbra to seek a spirit copy of the ring and use copious amounts of probably prime, spirit, forces, matter, and mind to be able to reform it in physical reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:03:10-07:00","id":1384500,"title":"","content":"Giving the ring a certain amount of intelligence to act on its own, and actually helps deal with some of the issues of modelling the powers of the ring, is to make it a Talisman type Wonder, since Talismans work on their own Arete rather than a mage's. The Book of Secrets expanded Wonder creation rules also has options for incorporating Backgrounds and Merits into Wonders to represent increased abilities.<br /> <br /> So, no, you don't need anything other than the Spheres to cast the effects, Prime 4, and a shit ton of magical resources as appropriate to your Focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:54:38-07:00","id":1386291,"title":"","content":"As a Storyteller, I would do this:<br /> <br /> You need to do the Green Lantern Effects, which mean that you need to do Prime 2, Forces 3, and Matter 4 [complex machinery] or Matter 2 [Simple Objects]<br /> <br /> To make a Green Lantern Ring, you need to have Prime 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:42:33-07:00","id":1386632,"title":"","content":"The ring rolls Arete 10 or the user's willpower, whichever is lower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T09:48:10-08:00","id":1432922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384384-making-a-green-lantern-ring?p=1384401#post1384401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real issue would be that there's no way to get around needing a certain number of successes to make certain (larger and/or more intricate) constructs, so you wouldn't be able to just produce anything and everything at a moment's notice. Otherwise, I think the most rudimentary version of the effect it would be (in M20 terms) Forces 3/Mind 3/Prime 2 effect--Forces 3/Prime 2 to generate not only the green light of the construct, but also the telekinetic power and <i>force</i> that makes it a &quot;hard light&quot; construct, and lasers; Mind 3 to control it all with your mind. The more legit version would be Forces 5/Mind 3/Prime 2, if only to scale up the power and &quot;oomph&quot; of the telekinesis component, enabling you to lift/withstand more. But you're still going to have the issue of not necessarily being able to generate in just one turn a huge locomotive, or a monstrous, Rob Liefeld/90's-esque laser cannon (as Kyle Raynor was so fond of doing).</div> </div> </div> </div>According to HDYDT, you only need Mind 3/Forces 3 to transform a mental image into a force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}